Implement a multi-stage arithmetic circuit that effectively computes a specific multiplication operation on a 32-bit input. This module takes a 32-bit input signal, performs a series of shifts and additions (specifically using left shifts and addition/subtraction of intermediate results) to produce a 32-bit output that corresponds to the modified multiplication result. The design leverages combinational logic to achieve the multiplication by using bitwise operations.
