description:
Design a 32-bit Linear Feedback Shift Register (LFSR) used for generating pseudorandom sequences. The module utilizes a clock and reset signal; when reset is activated, it initializes the shift register with a specific seed value. On each positive clock edge, the register shifts its contents to the left while computing a new feedback bit based on specific taps from the current state of the register (namely bits 31, 21, 1, and 0). This feedback bit is appended to the least significant position of the register, causing the register to evolve over time and produce a sequence of outputs that exhibit pseudorandom characteristics useful in applications like digital signal processing and cryptography.
module top_module(
data            ,  
clk             ,  
reset              
);

