description:
Design a clock divider circuit that reduces the frequency of an input clock signal. The module utilizes a counter that counts the number of clock cycles, and when the counter reaches its maximum value determined by the parameter BITS, it toggles the most significant bit to produce the output clock signal. The clock divider resets to zero when a reset signal is asserted, ensuring proper initialization. This design effectively creates a divided output clock frequency based on the input clock frequency.
module top_module(

   clock_out,

   clock_in, reset
   );

code:
module top_module(

   clock_out,

   clock_in, reset
   );parameter
     BITS = 3;

   output wire clock_out;

   input wire  clock_in, reset;

   reg [BITS-1:0]           counter;

   assign clock_out = counter[BITS-1];

   always @(posedge clock_in) begin
      if (reset) begin
         counter <= {BITS{1'd0}};
      end
      else begin
         counter <= counter + {{BITS-1{1'd0}}, 1'd1};
      end
   end

endmodule

